  The island of Enoshima, located southwest of Kamakura, is a major tourist attraction and the center of Benten worship in the Kanto region. A destination for pilgrims since the days of the Kamakura shogunate, the Edo period saw it equal Ise Shrine as an attraction for the pious.

  The island's unique scenery and atmosphere have remained much appreciated in the modern era, as advances in transportation have enabled tourists to visit from all over Yamato, and even the world.

  Among these tourists have been such venerable personages as Prince Ferdinand of Habsburg and General Nogi Maresuke. It is also notorious as the location where Dazai Osamu attempted suicide with his lover ten years ago, though this incident actually took place on Koyurugi Cape, on the opposite shore.

  In recent years, visitors have come for more than just religious observance or sightseeing. It is a popular fishing spot, for example, and has a variety of rare plants and animals to study.

  Its most recent attraction, however, bears special mention.

